export const LANDING_BODY = "<div id=\"top\" class=\"hero-wrap\"><div class=\"dots hero-dots-left\"></div><div class=\"dots hero-dots-right\"></div><div class=\"hero-panel\"><i class=\"cx tl\"></i><div style=\"position:absolute;inset:0;background:radial-gradient(ellipse 60% 45% at 50% 118%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--c-accent-fg) 18%, transparent), transparent 70%);pointer-events:none\"></div><div style=\"position:absolute;inset:0;background-image:radial-gradient(color-mix(in srgb, var(--c-text) 4.5%, transparent) 1px, transparent 1px);background-size:18px 18px;pointer-events:none\"></div><div class=\"hero-grid\"><div><div style=\"font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.22em;color:var(--c-accent);margin-bottom:24px\">THE SELF-EVOLVING AGENT PLATFORM</div><h1 style=\"font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(34px, 4.5vw, 58px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-.03em;margin:0 0 24px 0;text-wrap:pretty\">Agents that <span data-typewriter=\"true\" style=\"display:block;height:1.08em;white-space:nowrap;color:var(--c-accent)\">get better with use.<span data-caret=\"true\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"caret\"></span></span></h1><p style=\"font-size:17px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--c-text-2);margin-bottom:48px;text-wrap:pretty;margin:0 0 34px 0;max-width:540px\">Persistent workspaces with files, sessions, and memory. Hosted on Cloudflare, so tasks keep running after you close the laptop — or fully native on your machine, in the terminal or your editor.</p><div class=\"cmd\" style=\"max-width:560px\"><i class=\"cx tl\"></i><i class=\"cx br\"></i><code><span class=\"dollar\">$</span> @@INSTALL_COMMAND@@</code><button class=\"copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"landing-install-command\">COPY</button></div><div id=\"landing-install-command\" hidden=\"\">@@INSTALL_COMMAND@@</div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:18px;margin-top:24px;align-items:center\"><a href=\"/login\" class=\"btn solid\">TRY CLOUD AGENTS →</a><a href=\"#deploy\" class=\"btn\">DEPLOY YOUR OWN</a><span style=\"font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--c-text-3)\">MIT · open source</span></div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid var(--c-border);background:var(--c-sidebar);position:relative;padding:16px\"><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-bottom:8px;gap:12px\"><div data-hero-tabs=\"true\" style=\"display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:baseline\"><span style=\"font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.16em;color:var(--c-text-3)\">FIG.01</span><span role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-mode=\"optimise\" data-active=\"\" style=\"font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.16em;cursor:pointer;text-transform:uppercase;border-bottom:1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--c-accent) 50%, transparent);padding-bottom:2px\">optimise</span><span role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-mode=\"research\" style=\"font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.16em;cursor:pointer;text-transform:uppercase;border-bottom:1px solid transparent;padding-bottom:2px\">research</span><span role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-mode=\"ideate\" style=\"font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.16em;cursor:pointer;text-transform:uppercase;border-bottom:1px solid transparent;padding-bottom:2px\">ideate</span></div><span data-hero-status=\"true\" style=\"font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.16em;color:var(--c-accent)\"></span></div><canvas id=\"hero-tree\" width=\"1120\" height=\"880\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;display:block\"></canvas></div></div></div><div class=\"grid four claims\"><div class=\"claim\"><div class=\"stat-k\">LEARNS FROM USE</div><p>Every turn is graded against your next message. Lessons that later turns confirm persist.</p></div><div class=\"claim\"><div class=\"stat-k\">CRAFTS ITS OWN TOOLS</div><p>Recurring patterns become tools it builds, scores, and calls on its own.</p></div><div class=\"claim\"><div class=\"stat-k\">COMMANDS AGENT SWARMS</div><p>A hard task forks a scored tree of whole agents. The best attempt wins.</p></div><div class=\"claim\"><div class=\"stat-k\">YOUR CLOUD OR YOURS ALONE</div><p>Run it on kinu.run today, or deploy the same Worker into your own account.</p></div></div></div><section id=\"platform\" class=\"section\"><div class=\"label\">§ 01  THE PLATFORM</div><h2 style=\"margin:20px 0 16px 0;max-width:780px;margin-top:20px\">Close the laptop. <span class=\"gold\">The agent keeps working.</span></h2><p class=\"lede\" style=\"font-size:17px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--c-text-2);margin-bottom:48px;text-wrap:pretty;max-width:660px\">Kinu is a cloud-native agent platform on Cloudflare — workspaces and sandboxes are hosted, so a task you start keeps running after you close the browser. And the same agent runs fully native on your own machine.</p><div class=\"g two\"><div class=\"panel pad-32\"><i class=\"cx tl\"></i><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:14px\">IN THE CLOUD</div><h3>Hosted workspaces and sandboxes</h3><p style=\"font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--c-text-2);margin-top:12px\">Start a task, shut your computer, come back to the result. Agents live in Durable Objects and keep working in the background — schedules, webhooks, and email reach them while you&#x27;re away.</p></div><div class=\"panel pad-32\"><i class=\"cx br\"></i><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:14px\">ON YOUR MACHINE</div><h3>TUI, CLI, or your editor</h3><p style=\"font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--c-text-2);margin-top:12px\">Run it fully native and local: a full-screen TUI, a one-shot CLI, or inside your editor over ACP. The TUI also connects to your cloud agents — the terminal replaces the web UI whenever you prefer it.</p></div></div><div class=\"core-bar\">ONE BACKEND-AGNOSTIC CORE RUNS BOTH</div><div class=\"grid three hovers\"><div><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:12px\">RESEARCH, OVERNIGHT</div><p>Hand it a question in the evening. The brief, with sources, is waiting in the morning.</p></div><div><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:12px\">PRS REVIEWED IN THE BACKGROUND</div><p>A webhook wakes the agent on every pull request. The review is posted by the time you look.</p></div><div><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:12px\">PRS CREATED WHILE YOU&#x27;RE AWAY</div><p>Describe the change. The agent branches, builds, tests, and opens the pull request.</p></div></div></section><section id=\"quickstart\" class=\"section ruled-top\"><div class=\"label\">§ 02  QUICKSTART</div><h2 style=\"margin:20px 0 16px 0;max-width:800px;margin-top:20px\">Start in the cloud, <span class=\"gold\">or entirely on your own machines.</span></h2><p class=\"lede\" style=\"font-size:17px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--c-text-2);margin-bottom:48px;text-wrap:pretty;max-width:620px\">Both are the same core. Reach one workspace from the web app, the TUI, or the CLI.</p><div class=\"g three\"><div class=\"panel qs-card\"><i class=\"cx tl\"></i><div class=\"num\">IN THE BROWSER</div><h3>Web</h3><p class=\"qs-body\">Sign in and create a workspace. Nothing to install, and the same workspace opens from every client.</p><a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"/login\">SIGN IN →</a><div class=\"glimpse\" data-glimpse=\"web\"></div></div><div class=\"panel qs-card\"><div class=\"num\">IN THE TERMINAL</div><h3>TUI</h3><p class=\"qs-body\"><code style=\"color:var(--c-text);font-size:12px\">kinu chat</code> opens the full-screen app: pick a workspace, talk, and watch it work.</p><div class=\"mini-cmd\"><span class=\"dollar\">$</span> kinu chat triage</div><div class=\"glimpse\" data-glimpse=\"tui\"></div></div><div class=\"panel qs-card\"><i class=\"cx br\"></i><div class=\"num\">IN THE TERMINAL</div><h3>CLI</h3><p class=\"qs-body\">One command installs kinu on macOS or Linux. Create a workspace, then hand it a task.</p><div class=\"mini-cmd multi\"><span class=\"dollar\">$</span> @@INSTALL_COMMAND@@<br/><span class=\"dollar\">$</span> kinu create triage</div><div class=\"glimpse\" data-glimpse=\"cli\"></div></div></div><p class=\"dim\" style=\"margin-top:28px\">A workspace created anywhere opens from the others, with its files, sessions, and search history intact.</p></section><section id=\"clients\" class=\"section ruled-top\"><div class=\"label\">§ 03  ONE WORKSPACE, EVERY CLIENT</div><h2 style=\"margin:20px 0 16px 0;max-width:820px;margin-top:20px\">Work from the browser, the terminal, <span class=\"gold\">your editor, or email.</span></h2><p class=\"lede\" style=\"font-size:17px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--c-text-2);margin-bottom:48px;text-wrap:pretty;max-width:660px\">Every client opens the same workspace, with the same files and history. Start a run at your desk, check it over SSH from the terminal, read the result in your editor.</p><div class=\"grid four hovers\"><div><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:12px\">THE BROWSER</div><p>kinu.run shows your workspaces: files, sessions, and every search they have run.</p></div><div><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:12px\">THE TERMINAL</div><p><code style=\"color:var(--c-text);font-size:12px\">kinu chat</code> opens a conversation. <code style=\"color:var(--c-text);font-size:12px\">kinu run</code> executes one task and exits, for scripts and CI.</p></div><div><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:12px\">YOUR EDITOR</div><p><code style=\"color:var(--c-text);font-size:12px\">kinu acp</code> speaks the Agent Client Protocol, so editors like Zed can drive a workspace from a panel.</p></div><div><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:12px\">EMAIL</div><p>Each workspace has an email address. Mail to it starts a turn, and the reply arrives on the same thread. Not yet enabled on kinu.run.</p></div></div><div><figure class=\"film\">\n      <div class=\"anno ruled\"><span>CLI · kinu run · recorded 2026-08-21</span><span>workspace “film” · local backend</span></div>\n      <pre class=\"term\" id=\"cli-film\"><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"cmd\"><b>$</b> <span data-typed>kinu run film \"Find the slowest test in this repo and explain why it is slow.\"</span></span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"call\"><b>▸ run · workspace</b> cd /tmp/kinu-film-repo &amp;&amp; ls -la …</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"why\">The working directory /tmp/kinu-film-repo lives on the local machine, not the workspace filesystem.</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"call\"><b>▸ run · laptop</b> cd /tmp/kinu-film-repo &amp;&amp; ls -la &amp;&amp; echo \"---PKG---\" &amp;&amp; cat package.json …</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"why\">Read every source and test file to identify what each test does.</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"call\"><b>▸ run · laptop</b> cd /tmp/kinu-film-repo &amp;&amp; echo \"=== entries.ts ===\" &amp;&amp; cat -n src/entries.ts …</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"call\"><b>▸ run · laptop</b> cd /tmp/kinu-film-repo &amp;&amp; which bun &amp;&amp; bun --version &amp;&amp; echo \"===TEST===\" &amp;&amp; time bun test</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"out\"> 7 pass\n 0 fail\n 7 expect() calls\nRan 7 tests across 3 files. [912.00ms]</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"why\">Time each test file in isolation to isolate which test dominates the runtime.</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"out\">=== tests/parse.test.ts ===\n 3 pass\n 0 fail\nRan 3 tests across 1 file. [5.00ms]\n=== tests/dedupe.test.ts ===\n 2 pass\n 0 fail\nRan 2 tests across 1 file. [5.00ms]\n=== tests/summary.test.ts ===\n 2 pass\n 0 fail\nRan 2 tests across 1 file. [864.00ms]</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"why\">Measure dedupe runtime scaling at increasing input sizes to confirm quadratic growth.</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"out\">n=3000  dedupe=14.0ms\nn=6000  dedupe=43.8ms\nn=12000  dedupe=188.3ms\nn=24000  dedupe=827.3ms</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"call\"><b>▸ run · laptop</b> rm -f /tmp/bench.ts &amp;&amp; echo cleaned</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"why\">Remove the temporary benchmark file I created during investigation.</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"text\">## Slowest test</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"text\">**`summarizes a full season of unique readings`** in `tests/summary.test.ts` — it accounts for **~864 ms** of the suite's **~912 ms** total.</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"text\">## Why it is slow</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"text\">`dedupe` is **O(n²)**: for every entry it runs `kept.findIndex`, a linear scan over the array that has grown to hold all prior unique ids.</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"text\">Each doubling of the input roughly quadruples the runtime — the classic O(n²) fingerprint.</span><span class=\"line\" data-kind=\"text\">The fix, if wanted, is to dedupe with a `Map&lt;string, Entry&gt;` keyed by id (one pass, O(n)), keeping the same \"newest entry per id\" and first-seen-order semantics.</span></pre>\n      <div class=\"anno ruled\"><span>@cf/deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-pro-0813</span><span>10 steps · 264 s · live</span></div>\n    </figure></div><p class=\"dim\" style=\"margin-top:28px\">Schedules, webhooks, and finished background jobs start turns the same way.</p></section><section id=\"evolution\" class=\"section ruled-top\"><div class=\"label\">§ 04  SELF-EVOLUTION</div><h2 style=\"margin:20px 0 16px 0;max-width:760px;margin-top:20px\">Evolution <span class=\"gold\">on four timescales.</span></h2><p class=\"lede\" style=\"font-size:17px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--c-text-2);margin-bottom:48px;text-wrap:pretty;max-width:640px\">The shorter clocks feed the longer ones. None of it needs your upkeep: scoring, consolidation, and retirement run inside the workspace.</p><div class=\"grid four\"><div><div class=\"num\" style=\"margin-bottom:16px\">PER STEP · EVERY SETTLED TOOL CALL</div><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:10px\">TOOL FITNESS</div><p>Crafted tools are scored every time they run. Tools that keep failing drop out of the callable set mid-run.</p></div><div><div class=\"num\" style=\"margin-bottom:16px\">PER TURN · THE NEXT MESSAGE</div><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:10px\">TURN REVIEW</div><p>Each turn is graded against your next message. A lesson persists only when later turns corroborate it.</p></div><div><div class=\"num\" style=\"margin-bottom:16px\">PER SESSION · EVERY FIVE TURNS</div><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:10px\">CONSOLIDATION</div><p>Recurring patterns become reusable tools, and the agent can propose changes to its own loop. Proposals pass four structural gates and a shadow eval before they land.</p></div><div><div class=\"num\" style=\"margin-bottom:16px\">PER LIFETIME · EVERY FIVE WINDOWS</div><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:10px\">RETIREMENT AND SEARCH</div><p>Tool scores decay with time, and low scores retire the tool. <code style=\"color:var(--c-text);font-size:12px\">kinu evolve</code> searches over the loop itself, scored on graded turns.</p></div></div><p class=\"dim\" style=\"margin-top:28px\">Execution evidence feeds tool selection only. Nothing wider is promoted on it.</p></section><section id=\"swarm\" class=\"section ruled-top\"><div class=\"label\">§ 05  THE TREE OF AGENTS</div><div class=\"duo\" style=\"margin:20px 0 52px 0\"><div><h2 style=\"margin-bottom:16px\">Run one task <span class=\"gold\">as a tree of agents.</span></h2><p class=\"lede left\" style=\"margin-bottom:14px\">One tool call builds the tree. Each node is a whole agent that attempts the task its own way, in its own directory, with its own credential. Weak branches are pruned mid-run, and the winner answers.</p><p class=\"lede left\" style=\"margin-bottom:14px\">The agent turns your ask into an objective: a metric, a target, and a verifier. A verifier is code that runs in the workspace, and its number picks the winner.</p><p class=\"lede left\">What you get back is the winner plus the record: every branch, its score, and the verifier number behind each pick. Results persist per objective, so the next search starts from the record instead of from zero.</p></div><div class=\"well\" style=\"padding:24px 28px\"><i class=\"cx tr\"></i><div class=\"fig\" style=\"margin-bottom:16px\">FIG.03 · ONE CALL</div><div style=\"font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.9;color:var(--c-text-2)\">agents({<br/>  action: <span style=\"color:var(--c-accent-fg)\">&#x27;swarm&#x27;</span>, preset: <span style=\"color:var(--c-accent-fg)\">&#x27;optimise&#x27;</span>,<br/>  task: <span style=\"color:var(--c-accent-fg)\">&#x27;make the p95 faster&#x27;</span>,<br/>  objective: {<br/>    metric: <span style=\"color:var(--c-accent-fg)\">&#x27;p95_latency&#x27;</span>, unit: <span style=\"color:var(--c-accent-fg)\">&#x27;ms&#x27;</span>,<br/>    direction: <span style=\"color:var(--c-accent-fg)\">&#x27;down&#x27;</span>, target: <span style=\"color:var(--c-success)\">120</span>,<br/>    verifier: <span style=\"color:var(--c-accent)\">&#x27;bench.p95&#x27;</span> <span style=\"color:var(--c-text-3)\">// code, not a judge</span><br/>  }<br/>})</div><div style=\"border-top:1px dashed var(--c-border-strong);margin-top:18px;padding-top:14px;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:11px;line-height:1.9;color:var(--c-text-3)\">The shape follows the scenario: <span style=\"color:var(--c-accent)\">ideate</span> fans flat, <span style=\"color:var(--c-accent)\">optimise</span> climbs with UCT, <span style=\"color:var(--c-accent)\">prove</span> goes deepest, <span style=\"color:var(--c-accent)\">research · audit · redteam</span> cover a scored grid.</div></div></div><p class=\"dim\">The tree in the hero is the repo&#x27;s own search — switch its tabs to see each preset&#x27;s shape.</p></section><section id=\"deploy\" class=\"section ruled-top\"><div class=\"label\">§ 06  SELF-HOST</div><div class=\"duo\"><div><h2 style=\"margin-bottom:16px\">Host Kinu agents <span class=\"gold\">yourself.</span></h2><p class=\"lede left\" style=\"margin-bottom:32px\">The whole cloud platform deploys into your own Cloudflare account, backed by Durable Objects. Your agents, files, and model spend stay with you.</p><div class=\"actions start\"><a class=\"btn solid\" href=\"https://deploy.workers.cloudflare.com/?url=https://github.com/AshishKumar4/kinu\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">DEPLOY TO CLOUDFLARE →</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"https://github.com/AshishKumar4/kinu/blob/main/docs/SELF-HOSTING.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SELF-HOSTING GUIDE</a></div></div><div class=\"rows\"><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"fig\">STEP ONE</div><p><b>Bring the account.</b> Workers Paid plan, a zone, a wrangler login. Provisioning prints everything it cannot create for you.</p><div class=\"metric\">bun run infra:provision</div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"fig\">STEP TWO</div><p><b>Deploy, then provision again.</b> The deploy ships the Worker, its Durable Objects and its container. Secrets install on a Worker that exists.</p><div class=\"metric\">bun run deploy</div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"fig\">STEP THREE</div><p><b>Prove the account.</b> The infra gate checks every declared resource exists and the deployed Worker is bound to it. It exits non-zero when one is not.</p><div class=\"metric\">bun run gate:infra</div></div></div></div><div class=\"grid four\" style=\"margin-top:24px\"><div><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:12px\">UNLIMITED WORKSPACES</div><p>Workspaces are Durable Objects: nothing is billed while they sit idle — spend follows what runs and what you store, not how many workspaces you keep.</p></div><div><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:12px\">10 GB PER WORKSPACE</div><p>Every workspace keeps its own durable file plane — files, shell state, runtimes — on SQLite-backed storage (10 GB on Workers Paid, platform-catalog do.storage.bytes).</p></div><div><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:12px\">TRUE LINUX ON DEMAND</div><p>When an agent needs one, it attaches a full Linux sandbox on Cloudflare Containers.</p></div><div><div class=\"key\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:12px\">YOUR OWN DEVICES</div><p>Connect your PC and your agents can use it too — every access behind your consent.</p></div></div><p class=\"dim\" style=\"margin-top:28px;max-width:900px\">When the infra gate passes, the Worker serving your requests is the same one kinu.run runs.</p></section><section id=\"cta\" class=\"cta-band\"><div class=\"duo cta-grid\"><div><div class=\"label\">§ 07  OPEN SOURCE</div><h2 style=\"margin:20px 0 18px 0\">Open source, <span class=\"gold\">end to end.</span></h2><p class=\"lede left\" style=\"max-width:520px;margin-bottom:36px\">MIT-licensed — the agent, both backends, and the CLI.</p><div class=\"actions start\"><a class=\"btn solid\" href=\"https://github.com/AshishKumar4/kinu\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">READ THE SOURCE →</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"/login\">TRY CLOUD AGENTS</a></div></div><div class=\"well spec-well\"><i class=\"cx tl\"></i><i class=\"cx br\"></i><div class=\"spec-row\"><div class=\"fig\">LICENCE</div><div style=\"font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:12px\">MIT</div></div><div class=\"spec-row\"><div class=\"fig\">SOURCE</div><div style=\"font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:12px\"><a href=\"https://github.com/AshishKumar4/kinu\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">github.com/AshishKumar4/kinu</a></div></div><div class=\"spec-row\"><div class=\"fig\">BACKENDS</div><div style=\"font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:12px\">Cloudflare Workers · POSIX</div></div><div class=\"spec-row last\"><div class=\"fig\">DOCS</div><div style=\"font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:12px;display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap\"><a href=\"https://github.com/AshishKumar4/kinu/blob/main/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">architecture</a><a href=\"https://github.com/AshishKumar4/kinu/blob/main/docs/EXPLORATION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">exploration</a><a href=\"https://github.com/AshishKumar4/kinu/blob/main/docs/EVOLUTION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">evolution</a><a href=\"https://github.com/AshishKumar4/kinu/blob/main/docs/DEPLOYMENT.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">deployment</a></div></div></div></div></section>";
